      "file": "content/reader-papers/when-institutional-programs-work-together.md",
      "old": "An independent-choice cell is a collection of local menus whose every combination satisfies the complete joint relation. The menus contain complete continuation policies, including their possible outcomes. Their product must remain admissible under the fixed request and history \\[[1](#ref-linking){style=\"overflow-wrap:anywhere;hyphens:none\"}, Section 8\\]. Selecting a menu does not itself acquire its resources.",
      "new": "An independent-choice cell is a collection of local menus whose every combination satisfies the complete joint relation. The menus contain complete continuation policies, including their possible outcomes. Their product must remain admissible under the fixed request and history \\[[1](#ref-linking){style=\"overflow-wrap:anywhere;hyphens:none\"}, Section 10\\]. Selecting a menu does not itself acquire its resources.",
